  <!--=====T2 CUSTODIAN=====-->

  <ThingDef ParentName="TreeBase">    <!--todo: add zone growth coding and add building coding-->
    <defName>ET_BuildingTreeTierTwo</defName>
    <label>Grovetender Tree</label>
    <description>The Grovetender Tree is the evolution of the Primwood Custodian Tree. It boasts a larger terraforming radius and higher resilience, but also takes longer to grow, and is highly sensitive to terrain. Proper terrain can be created by the Primwood Custodian, effectively enabling Elderwood-type trees in any colony.
Like other Conduit trees, abundant space is required between each one of the same kind. However, it can be placed close to a Custodian tree, and both will work in tandem.
\nGrovetender vs Custodian differences:
Terraforming radius: 5 (Custodian: 3)
Terraforming speed: 2 tiles/day (Custodian: 1)
Fertility requirement: 80% (Custodian: 5%)
Growing time: 4 full days (Custodian: 2)</description>
    <drawerType>MapMeshAndRealTime</drawerType>
